# Polaris Docker build context filter.
#
# Keeps `docker build` snappy and reproducible by pruning everything the
# multi-stage Dockerfiles do not need. The builder stage runs
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm --filter <name> build` from the
# repository root, so the build context must include source, package.json
# files, pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml, and TypeScript configs — and
# nothing else of size or sensitivity.
#
# Conventions:
#   - Negation patterns (`!path`) are only used to re-include items beneath a
#     broader exclusion. We avoid them where a plain include is enough.
#   - Test artifacts and tests themselves are excluded; production images do
#     not need them, and tsconfig.json files reference test sources via the
#     `tests` rootDir which the builder image installs anyway.

# Node / pnpm install artifacts. The builder stage runs a fresh install.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store

# Build outputs. Always re-emitted by `pnpm --filter <name> build`.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test artifacts and snapshots.
coverage
**/coverage
.vitest
**/.vitest
**/__snapshots__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts

# VCS metadata. `POLARIS_GIT_SHA` is passed in as a build arg instead.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local environment files. Production secrets are injected at runtime.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor / OS scratch.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea
.vscode

# Claude Code worktree / session state.
.claude

# Local-only ops files that have no business in a runtime image.
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
README.md
USAGE.md
docs
sql
scripts/smoke
tests
resources/maxmind

# `definitions` is not on that list, and cannot go back on it.
#
# It was, from `9a5da8d` until the commit that removed it -- under its former
# name `catalog`, which `0DIPB` retired -- and the reason was good at the
# time: the directory held declared YAML that no shipped code read. It is source now, in two separate ways, and each one breaks a build
# on its own.
#
#   - Five subdirectories are pnpm workspace packages -- `definitions/traits`,
#     `definitions/policy`, `definitions/audiences`, `definitions/journeys`,
#     `definitions/reverse-etl`. apps/ingester-api, apps/polaris-cli,
#     async/journeys/orchestrator/v1 and packages/destination-host depend on
#     them with `workspace:*`, so the builder cannot compile those images
#     without the directory present.
#   - `definitions/projects/<id>.yaml` carries the per-project identity and
#     enrichment overrides -- the identifier denylist among them -- which
#     sync/identity/resolver/v1 and sync/enrichment/runtime/v1 COPY out of
#     the builder into the runtime image.
#
# The second one is what caught us: the exclusion and the COPY were written
# three months apart, each correct alone, and together they left two images
# unbuildable for six days without anything saying so. `pnpm lint` now runs
# `scripts/lint-docker-context.mjs`, which fails when a Dockerfile copies a
# path this file prunes.

# Per-package READMEs and changelogs are not needed in the image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
